{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/281172-the-related-themes-of-mummy-and-demon-mummy-st-spoilers","id":281172,"title":"The related themes of Mummy and Demon (Mummy ST spoilers)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-14T09:47:39-07:00","id":281172,"title":"The related themes of Mummy and Demon (Mummy ST spoilers)","content":"Or: why Demon and Mummy are my favorite nWoD games.<br /> <br /> Mummy and Demon definitely have very different aesthetics - the former is wrapped in dark pulp and Egyptian imagery and the latter is a weird blend between angelic mythology, techgnosticism, and the spy genre.<br /> <br /> Both deal with freedom and servitude from different angles. Mummy looks at the themes through class struggle, while Demon looks at freedom as a kind of apostasy. <br /> <br /> In Mummy, you play a former middle class artisan, who still works for incomprehensible overlords - the 42 Judges of Duat - and fights off attacks from resentful members of the lower classes. Obedient labor crushes the Arisens' identity by blurring their memories. Freedom can be achieved by strengthening the self, and rebuilding one's identity. It is even rumored that one can break entirely free from servitude to the Judges.<br /> <br /> In Demon, you start out having rebelled against your creator. Like Mummy's Judges, the God-Machine still needs its faithful servants, so it is constantly trying to recapture its former agents, necessitating that the demons disguise themselves as humans and attempt to live nondescript lives. Unlike Mummies, Demon protagonists (barring a prelude) start free from control, but freedom is fragile and can only be maintained by constant vigilance bordering on extreme paranoia. The various agendas that Demons hold are also reminiscent of the various viewpoints apostates hold to their former belief or association. Saboteurs want to bring down the God-Machine, Inquisitors want to know everything about it, Tempters just want to live full lives away from it, and Integrators want to negotiate a way back in to its good graces, but without giving up their hard fought freedoms. <br /> <br /> I don't want to try to retool these games so that Mummies who achieve Apotheosis become Demons, but I do think that it might be worthwhile to play a Mummy chronicle and then immediately follow it up with a Demon chronicle, since the themes of each game reinforce each other. Perhaps freedom and identity might seem especially fragile and valuable when your previous characters suffered under oppressive rule in a previous game. <br /> <br /> Any Thoughts? Are there any other games that go well together in this sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:01:26-07:00","id":281190,"title":"","content":"Those are some pretty good points, I never thought to compare the two before. I agree that they both have a very strong theme about becoming your own master. In that light, Apotheosis can be seen as a kind of Hell, really.<br /> <br /> As for other lines, I'd say Mummy also works very well as a sort of dark mirror of Mage. People (including Dave) have pointed out the similarity between the Pillars and the Subtle arcana and how they both make up the soul. Exarchs ascended, Shan'iatu descended. A Mage's growth climaxes in them becoming all powerful gods over the fabric of reality and finally becoming their own masters, a Mummy's growth climaxes in them letting go of their god powers and finally becoming their own masters. They deal with a lot of similar ideas, but they go about them from opposite directions and its pretty interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:05:22-07:00","id":281215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/281172-the-related-themes-of-mummy-and-demon-mummy-st-spoilers?p=281190#post281190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are some pretty good points, I never thought to compare the two before. I agree that they both have a very strong theme about becoming your own master. In that light, Apotheosis can be seen as a kind of Hell, really.<br /> <br /> As for other lines, I'd say Mummy also works very well as a sort of dark mirror of Mage. People (including Dave) have pointed out the similarity between the Pillars and the Subtle arcana and how they both make up the soul. Exarchs ascended, Shan'iatu descended. A Mage's growth climaxes in them becoming all powerful gods over the fabric of reality and finally becoming their own masters, a Mummy's growth climaxes in them letting go of their god powers and finally becoming their own masters. They deal with a lot of similar ideas, but they go about them from opposite directions and its pretty interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points about the Shan'iatu. There's a neat merit in Imperial Myteries that allows archmasters to control cabals and even entire cities worth of mages as their pawns. It might be worthwhile to go from a high level game like that straight into Mummy. The party would go from being the master wizard manipulators to the pawns of the same.<br /> <br /> Edit: Not equating the Shan'iatu to archmages in anything but theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:08:43-07:00","id":281401,"title":"","content":"Mummy is Old Age to Promethean's Childhood. Both games are, like all WoD games, about the human experience, but from different perspectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T13:16:22-07:00","id":281407,"title":"","content":"Ah, good call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:43:38-07:00","id":281496,"title":"","content":"As a side note, a mixed group of demons and mummies is a very effective group. We have a demon and mummy pair. While the Mummy's memory can fail, the demon's cannot. A demon can be fragile, while a Mummy only is at its lowest point. A newly risen mummy can protect a demon from angels, and the demon can keep the mummy hidden and safe as it nears henet. If shit hits the fan, the demon can go loud. The cult of the mummy can be a source of soul contracts, as mummies usually can stand to lose a human. Plus, utterances are very biblical. The Process &quot;memory theft&quot; is strange--the demon wife uses it to remove and &quot;store&quot; important flashbacks for the mummy. And as the OP said, their themes don't interfere with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T14:48:46-07:00","id":281503,"title":"","content":"Hmm, the games' respective themes mesh well, but I can certainly imagine devout Arisen being horrified at the Demons' renunciation of their divine duty. I can certainly imagine them working well together, at least in a mercenary sense. Demons can promise quite a bit of help in return for pacts with Arisen cultists. Just...don't bring your pet cryptid with you, as it might be easily mistaken for a Lifeless Amkhata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T15:51:50-07:00","id":281541,"title":"","content":"The one thing that came to my mind as <b>Demon</b> became more spoiled was that it was about divine servitors who had already fallen whereas, in a game focused on Apotheosis, <b>Mummy</b> was about divine servitors in the <i>process of</i> falling. You know?<br /> <br /> And <b>Promethean</b> was about supernatural creatures learning to become human, whereas <b>Mummy</b> was about <i>remembering</i> to be human. I suppose <b>Vampire</b> is about becoming <i>inhuman</i> and <b>Demon</b> is about 'fake it til you make it.'<br /> <br /> In a crossover game? A Mummy's tomb is a perfect ley-line of God-machine infrastructure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}